# =============================================================================
# Confidentiality first.
#
# Real lease data must never reach this repo or its history: no client rents,
# addresses, party names, site names, FANs, or executed documents.
#
# The policy is deny-by-default for the formats that carry deal data, with a
# narrow allowlist for the few files that are demonstrably synthetic or are
# published market research. If you are adding an exception, the test is not
# "is this useful" but "would I be comfortable with this file being public".
# =============================================================================

# ---- Office and PDF: deny by default -----------------------------------------
# Executed leases, amendments, audit worksheets, correspondence and trackers all
# arrive as these. The amendment template in particular stores *cached merge
# results* inline -- a real landlord name, site address, site name, FAN, rent
# and escalator sit inside the .docx even when no merge has been run. Clause
# text is extracted to clauses/text/*.txt with merge fields as placeholders;
# the .docx itself stays out.
*.docx
*.doc
*.dotx
*.xlsx
*.xlsm
*.xltx
*.xls
*.pptx
*.ppt
*.pdf

# NO EXCEPTIONS. The market rent schedule used to be tracked here as the sole
# authoring surface for the tier model. It is not any more:
#
#   - a compiled rate table is commercially valuable, and this repository is public
#   - it made Excel a dependency of a project whose whole premise is that it
#     opens from disk with nothing installed
#   - it stored derived values beside their own inputs, which is how five adder
#     columns came to be computed from a baseline, unused by the tool, and free
#     to drift out of agreement with it
#
# market/market-rates.json replaces it: inputs only, bands computed at load.
# See docs/market-data.md.

# ---- Your own market rates ---------------------------------------------------
# The shipped market/market-rates.json is ILLUSTRATIVE and deliberately
# conservative. A real one is yours; keep it out of here.
*.rates.json
market-rates.private.json
market-rates.local.json

# ---- Real deal files ---------------------------------------------------------
# Saved projects from the comparator and audit tool describe actual sites.
# Only the synthetic fixtures are tracked.
# Note the trailing /* rather than /. Excluding the DIRECTORY would make the
# README un-re-includable — git cannot rescue a file whose parent directory is
# excluded. Excluding the contents leaves the directory itself visible.
deals/*
!deals/README.md
*.deal.json
!fixtures/*.json

# ---- Source documents --------------------------------------------------------
# Scanned leases and amendments staged for an audit.
source-documents/
*.tif
*.tiff

# ---- Office lock files -------------------------------------------------------
~$*
.~lock.*

# ---- OS and editor -----------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# ---- Scratch -----------------------------------------------------------------
_probe/
scratch/
tmp/
